{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 10.903,
   "text": "I spent last summer alone in a fire lookout tower, sixty feet up. The only way in is a trapdoor in the floor."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 11.603,
   "end": 18.28,
   "text": "The ranger who drove me up tapped the latch and said, After dark, this stays shut. No matter who's knocking."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 19.08,
   "end": 22.877,
   "text": "I laughed. The nearest road was eleven miles away."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 23.877,
   "end": 29.808,
   "text": "On my third night, I saw a flashlight down in the pines... moving slowly toward the tower."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 30.708,
   "end": 35.508,
   "text": "Then the stairs started creaking. One step at a time... all the way up."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 38.108,
   "end": 41.585,
   "text": "Something knocked on the trapdoor. Three times."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 44.185,
   "end": 49.177,
   "text": "Then the ranger's voice said my name. Storm's rolling in, kid. Let me up."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 50.177,
   "end": 53.825,
   "text": "My hand was on the latch... when I looked out the window."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 55.025,
   "end": 60.615,
   "text": "No clouds. Just stars, all the way to the mountains. And no headlights on the road."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 61.615,
   "end": 66.777,
   "text": "So I sat on that trapdoor until the knocking stopped... and the stairs went quiet."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 67.977,
   "end": 71.007,
   "text": "I was still shaking when I heard it again."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 73.207,
   "end": 77.303,
   "text": "A soft tap... on the glass behind me. Sixty feet up."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 78.703,
   "end": 83.076,
   "text": "And the ranger's voice whispered, That's fine. I'll wait up here."
  }
 ],
